  READING: the constraint is VALID but WEAK here -- the excluded fraction of pairs is
  ~1e-2 or less, because short common prefixes are typical, so the lcp-restricted bound
  is barely below the trivial |V|^2 and far above the true sum h^2.  The lemma supplies
  real arithmetic information (it kills exactly the long-shared-prefix pairs) but does
  NOT by itself deliver (*): it removes a vanishing fraction of the pair count, whereas
  (*) needs sum h^2 near |V|^2/q.  Recorded as a precise negative.
